# produces folders with useful information all inside the Outputs/ folder, in short summarises all genomes by the cog numbers in each category in config.py
	#All_Features_per_Genome has all prokka features found in each genome that match any of the COGs provided, and the respective amino acid and DNA sequence 
	#Transposed holds intermediate files with only the number of PFAM hits per prokka feature per genome
	#Genomes_with_PFAM_list holds files similar to those in All_Features_per_Genome/, but with the PFAM hits of each prokka feature discriminated as well
	#All_Genomes_grouped_features.csv is an overview table, with the information from All_Features_per_Genome grouped together
	#PFAM_grouped_table.csv holds the counts of all PFAMs found only in the COGs provided, as well as the sums by row (number of pfams in the gene) and by column (counts of that PFAM domain in all genomes). 


python batch_make_fasta_for_Tree.py
